# Runtime state — regenerated, never committed
data/snapshots/
data/secrets/
data/feeds/
data/**/*.db
data/*.db
*.log

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# repo". That was true when it was a straight copy. It stopped being
# true the moment we started EDITING it -- wiring in ops skills at R2,
# and trimming it at R9.
#
# The cost showed up immediately: four skill files were deleted during
# the R9 trim with no way to undo, because nothing was tracking them.
# They were recoverable only because the untouched source at
#
# data/backups hold real conversation content, 18 MB of it, which is
# personal and does not belong in a repository that may be published.
# (data/* not data/: git cannot re-include a file inside an ignored
# DIRECTORY, only inside an ignored glob)
# ...except the GUI: console.html is code that happens to live under
# data/. Excluding it wholesale is the same mistake that once shipped
# a disc without its knowledge base.

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.iso

# Disk images used by the live boot harnesses. Test fixtures, not source:
# 93 MB of them reached a commit before this rule existed.
*.vhdx
*.vhd
*.qcow2
*.img
*.raw
*.vmdk

# Network Guard runtime state — regenerated by census/expose/patrol/dashboard,
# machine-specific (device MACs/IPs), same rule as data/snapshots/.
data/census/

# The registered administrator. Holds the ntfy topic (which IS the
# secret: anyone who knows it receives the alerts) and mail settings.
# data/admin.example.json is the tracked template.
data/admin.json

# Each host's current view of the LAN — machine-specific device MACs,
# same rule as data/snapshots/. The SHARED copy of this folder is how
# two machines corroborate; neither belongs in git.
data/census/observations/

# The confirmed Wi-Fi radios for THIS location. Machine-specific and
# location-revealing (BSSIDs geolocate), same rule as data/snapshots/.
data/census/wifi_baseline.json

# The machine that owns this data directory. Machine-specific state:
# committing it would ship one hostname to every clone, and the next
# checkout would be refused on its own first run.
data/OWNER.json

# Archived contamination (2026-07-27) — quarantined evidence, not content.
# It was committed by an over-broad `git add -A`; runtime state and
# incident debris do not belong in history.
data/_contamination-archive-20260727/
